I’m building the front end for the Outcome 4 code-a-thon experiments (Nov 17–19) on spine surgery in-basket questions. Context:

Service: pre-surgery-app, Python FastAPI on Cloud Run, project dpe-pre-surgery-d, program dpe-poc. All routes are under /pre-surgery, and the API is under /pre-surgery/api. Deploy workflow: .github/workflows/deploy-dev.yml.
App: five screens in one page: Anticipate (trigger → top five questions), Answer (question → cluster handling and answer), Gather (follow-up questions → clinician handoff summary), Ask your own, and Chat.
Files: main.py, data.py, chat.html, question_bank.json (45 Appendix A questions), gather_flows.json (12 flows), tests/test_app.py.
Rules to keep: no patient data. Cluster C, routing and unassigned questions never show an AI answer. Mixed clusters take the stricter reading. Every Gather flow ends in a handoff. Don’t invent clinical answers, intent, acuity or frequency.
Next: check the Dockerfile copies all five app files, run the tests, run locally with uvicorn, then push and deploy to dev. After that, wire in real experiment results by filling the null fields in question_bank.json.
Open items: access control before any live data, the Apigee PSC ticket, and the Akamai hostname.
